# Regression test for known-issues #7 (fixed): parse_primary() built the
# `myon.*` qualified-name path with the same unchecked accumulation pattern as
# #6, but into a 128-byte buffer -- so a long `myon.a.b.c...` chain wrote out of
# bounds while parsing.
#
# Like #6 this triggered at *parse* time (`--compile`, no execution).  An
# over-long qualified name must now be a plain syntax error (non-zero exit),
# never a buffer overflow.
#
# Only the non-zero exit is pinned, not the exact message text.
